exports[`habits: every reply, word for word > what the listing says on WhatsApp 1`] = `
{
  "groupName": "🌱 Habits",
  "help": "*Habits*

_add meditate_ starts a habit
_habits_ shows your streaks
_done meditate_ logs it for today, _undo meditate_ takes it back
_stop meditate_ stops tracking it
_time meditate morning_ moves a habit to the morning poll (6am), _time meditate default_ puts it back
_add stretch in the morning_ adds a habit to the morning poll
_time morning_ asks about every habit in the morning unless it is marked otherwise, _time evening_ in the evening, _time off_ stops the polls
_add gym on mon wed fri_ adds a habit for some days only
_days gym tue thu_ changes its days, _days gym every day_ puts it back
_simple on_ makes my check-in just the habit's name and streak, and lets you send just the name to log it. _simple off_ turns it off
_delete polls on_ deletes a one-habit poll once you answer it. _delete polls off_ keeps it

*More groups:* _new group gym buddies_ makes another Habits group, for a different set of habits or of people
_groups_ lists yours, _close group gym buddies_ ends one

*With other people:* add anyone to any Habits group. They can answer a habit's poll to do it with you, or add habits of their own. Everyone sees who did what on the poll, and _habits_ shows everyone's streaks

Twice a day I send one poll with the habits that are due: morning habits at 6am, evening ones at 8pm. Once I see when you usually answer, I send it around then. Tick what you did. You can tick more, or take a tick back, until the next day's poll. When only one habit is due I ask about it with Yes or No.",
  "welcome": "🌱 You've installed *Habits*.

Tell me a habit you want to build, in your own words, or send _add meditate_. Every day I'll send a poll with your habits, in the evening (8pm): tick the ones you did.

Send _help_ any time.",
}
`;
